Z||000005||87GTZ34||08-31-2001||08:04 AM||||Montana,  I don't have a 3.4 PR (mines a DOHC) engine but I think I know what you need.  You need to get a brass fitting that threads into pipe in place of the plug in the upper left circle that you've drawn.  The other side should be a compression fitting and the sender extension pipe will fit onto it.  Good auto parts stores have a stock of these brass items in the brake fitting section.  On my 2.8, the previous owner's mechanic had over tightened this (he was hercules) and it had a crack that leaked so I replaced mine and this is how I know.  The dealer said it is a non-serviceable item and directed me to a local parts store where 'they' buy from.  For the filter you need a male to male adapter (no jokes please).  I think auto stores carry them as well as home improvement stores.  No sealer or lube tape on the filter nipple and use the red rtv high temp, oil resistant sealer on the threads of the pressure sender fitting.  Use a thin coat and let it dry (24hrs) and put anther thin coat on before you put it in.  Do not over tighten this as it is easy to do (brass into cast iron). Also, you may need to use the plug you removed previously (in front) next to where the filter will screw on.  If you can remove the current filter adapter and post a picture, I can tell you definitively.  GL||||reg||1
